Yes. The right way to build this is as a **canonical visual asset system with autonomous generation, validation, reuse, and versioning**.

The goal is not:

```text
prompt → image → use once
```

It is:

```text
GAME STATE / CANON
↓
VISUAL SPEC
↓
ASSET GENERATOR
↓
CANDIDATES
↓
VALIDATION
↓
CANONICAL ASSET VERSION
↓
ASSET GRAPH
↓
SHOT COMPILER
↓
IMAGE / VIDEO / UI / POSTER / THUMBNAIL
↓
REUSE
```

The asset library becomes part of RoboBladez’s persistent world state.

# 1. Core principle

Every persistent thing in RoboBladez should have **two representations**:

```text
STRUCTURAL STATE
what it actually is

VISUAL STATE
how that thing currently appears
```

For example:

```text
BORIS_TALISMAN_R17
```

has:

```text
mechanical spec:
mass
radius
contact geometry
abilities
materials class
affinity

visual spec:
silhouette
surface materials
markings
palette
motifs
damage state
Daimon influence
```

The mechanical object is canonical gameplay truth.

The visual object is canonical presentation truth.

Neither should be reconstructed from prose every time.

